# Every way a tier-1 operation succeeds that no refused claim covers, that is not exempt and that
# is not an entry the operations it reaches cover, as tools/check-refused.py --coverage finds them
# (design/refused-claim-per-way/).
# The gate's unrefused step fails unless these lines are exactly the report's lines whose claim is
# none. A change that covers a way removes its line in the same commit. Adding a line lowers what
# the check shows, so it is a decision only the human can make: tools/land.py refuses a landing
# that adds one unless --approve names it, as path:operation:way.
# Fields, separated by tabs: path from the repository root, operation, way.
#
